*Heading
** Cohesive mass probe. One solid element and one zero-thickness cohesive element, every
** node given 1 m/s along x, so the initial kinetic energy is half the mass and the mass
** convention for a zero-thickness cohesive element can be read off directly.
** Solid mass alone is 1650 * 1e-3 * 1e-3 * 5e-4 = 8.25e-7 kg, so a kinetic energy of
** 4.13e-7 J means the cohesive element contributed nothing, while 8.25e-4 J means its
** mass was computed from the constitutive thickness of 1.0 m instead of the zero
** geometric thickness.
